ith their initials in the middle  a moment which reminded me of how lj  painted a blue heart on a lantern after  their first real date in the second  movie  and those blue hearts in both films fit  perfectly with the trilogy's colour  palette  which relies heavily on cyans as well as  magentas and yellows  as we can see from the characters  clothes as well as the film sets props  and cinematography  and those signature colors magenta cyan  and yellow  are the same ones that the filmmakers  used to light the empire state building  for the new york rooftop party scene  when peter surprises the cubbies after  they get back from korea kitty  compliments him on his welcome home sign  your spatial planning could use a bit of  work but i appreciate the glitter  which is a nice nod to this moment in  the second movie where kitty used  glitter for the valentine's card she  secretly sent to mrs roth's child on  behalf of her dad  dad's not a glitter type of guy nor were  you a peter kavinsky kind of girl to  sprinkle some glitter on it genevieve  complimenting lara jean's footwear and  always and forever  oh my god cute shoes i like this it's a  call back to how jen commented  sarcastically on lj's boots in the first  movie  cute boots thank you so much for your  service  notice how lara jean and genevieve's  position in the hallway has been  switched around this time  making this moment a mirror of the  original scene and showing how they are  both back to being friends now  rather than the antagonists they were at  the start of the first film  author jenny han's cameo in each of the  movies has become a tradition  and in always and forever she makes a  brief appearance in the flashback scene  of lj and pk's meek cute  han is principal cho who calls lara jean  on stage to receive an attendance award  according to the filmmakers her  appearances as a middle school principal  in the first and third movies  and as alder high's vice principal in  the second movie give her  character a mini career arc across the  trilogy  by the way the same crying girl that  jenny han was comforting on valentine's  day and p.s i still love you has a much  happier moment in always and forever  when she's the recipient of a musical  promposal molly marshall will you go to  prom with me  yes of course when lj organizes a  perfect date with peter she takes some  inspiration from the classic koen  brothers crime comedy the big lebowski  and plans an evening at a local bowling  alley where she sets their table with  some tasty treats for them to eat  including the same kind of fruit  turnover she made for peta as a  valentine's day gift in the second movie  when lara jean is planning the perfect  date she compiles a list of some of  peter's favorite films for ideas  it's mostly made up of action movies  like fast and furious but an interesting  one is x-men apocalypse because that's  the film in which lana condor made her  acting debut as the mutant jubilee  this is scott he's new here too  and this might be a little stretch but  the movie this is the end has been  crossed out  perhaps foreshadowing that although  always and forever is a final movie in  the series this won't be the end of lj  and pk's story  as they choose to stay together at  university despite the many miles  between them  owen doctor's sleep appears on the list  as the director of the second and third  to all the boys films michael ferminari  was the cinematographer on that movie  butterflies keep cropping up in the new  film from the poster and lara jean's  english classroom  to various knickknacks in her bedroom to  the ones on lockers at school  culturally butterflies are often symbols  of transformation  freedom and new beginnings all themes  that are crucial in the final film  as lara jean is on the verge of a new  life making big decisions that will take  her from her final days as a schoolgirl  to her new future as a university  student  which is why we also see a large  butterfly poster as well as a follow  your heart poster in margot's college  room in scotland as she's already making  her own life for herself and encourages  lj to do the same  as well as butterflies pointing to the  theme of change in lj's life the film is  full of posters that foreshadow her  decision to choose new york university  over berkeley  even before lj knows that she's been  accepted to nyu  at school there are new york posters  with the statue of liberty all around  peter  and as they all hand in their permission  slips for the east coast trip  we see posters including one with the  words how far will you go  a drawing of a woman with a question  mark over her head signaling how lj will  question her decision about university  and a poster of another woman with the  words own your story which feels  especially fitting because as lj's dad  later tells her  listen laura jean you gotta stay true to  yourself you can't save this  relationship by not growing  likewise when lj's struggling to decide  whether she should follow her desire to  go to nyu  and asks jen whether she should go she's  standing next to posters that feature  the statue of liberty  the words do what you love and you are  stronger than you think  the fabric box that lara jean fills with  memories of their relationship and gives  to peter  is actually the same box that held lj's  letters to all the boys she'd loved  before  which gives the box extra emotional  value because it was instrumental in how  lj and peter's relationship began  after laura jean accidentally texts  peter that she got into stamford to  celebrate he turns up outside her house  recreating the iconic scene from say  anything the 80s rom-com where the male  lead holds up a boom box to prove his  love there's this great scene with john  cusack and he sits underneath the window  and he holds up a boom  lara jean's love of classic 80s movies  has been a hallmark of her story in this  trilogy from her recreation of the  opening scene of 